	"reviewNotes": [
		"Ethnic attributions follow the cited biographies. Where a biography gives only a birthplace, the people is inferred from it and marked medium; where even that is unclear, the people is shown as “Not recorded”.",
		"The 1967 borders are drawn from today’s LGAs. Kogi is split: its Igala LGAs (Idah, Dekina, Ankpa and the rest) are shown in Benue-Plateau, the old Kabba Province in Kwara. The Federal Capital Territory, carved out in 1976 from Niger, Plateau and Kwara, is shown whole in North-Western State.",
		"In the Mid-West, Biafra’s Albert Okonkwo ran the state from August to September 1967; he is not listed as a governor."
	],
